{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Et the Kenite and et the Kenizzite and et the Kadmonite.</b> Rashi: they are Ammon and Moab and Edom, and they are destined to be an inheritance in the future. <b>Et the Kenite</b> — he is Ammon, as is explained in the portion of Balak. And et the Kenizzite — he is Moab. <b>And et the Kadmonite</b> — he is Edom, on account of Amalek that came forth from him, who was first (קדמוני) to engage Israel in battle, as it is written: ״ראשית גוים עמלק״. Rabbi Chelbo said in the name of Rabbi Yochanan: thus it arose in the mind of HaShem to give ten nations to Israel as an inheritance, but He gave them only seven; but Kenite, Kenizzite, and Kadmonite He did not give them. And when will He give them to them? In the days of the Messiah. Even so, through the exaction of tribute some of these years came into their hands — that is, parts of the lands of the children of Ammon and Moab, in the war against Sichon and Og."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The text spells the third nation קדמני in the lemma and comment, but קדמוני in the body; both forms rendered as they appear. טרוניא rendered as 'exaction of tribute' per its Talmudic usage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:24.341946964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}